**Scenario**

An order is paid and sitting in the Shipping Department.  The warehouse has not printed a label yet, and the customer
asks to cancel the order and get a full refund.

The UltraCart part is a single call: `PUT /order/orders/{order_id}/refund` with `reject_after_refund=true`.  This is the
API version of the "Complete Refund (then reject)" button in the backend.  It refunds the order to the original payment
method and moves the order out of the Shipping Department into Rejected.  No separate cancel call is needed.

1. `GET /order/orders/{order_id}`: confirm `current_stage` is `Shipping Department` and `shipping.tracking_numbers` is empty.
2. `GET /order/orders/{order_id}/refundable`: confirm `refundable` is `true` (treat null as false).
3. Cancel the order at your fulfillment provider.
   - Using ShipStation with "Cancel in ShipStation on Full Refund" set to Yes on the distribution center's transport
     mechanism?  Skip this step.  After the full refund in step 4, UltraCart automatically tells ShipStation to cancel
     the order.  Test this end to end on a test order before relying on it.  If ShipStation refuses (a label already
     exists), the refund has already happened.  UltraCart records the refusal as a warning in the distribution center log.
   - Otherwise, cancel the order at your fulfillment provider **first**.  If it refuses because a label already exists,
     stop and do not refund.
4. `PUT /order/orders/{order_id}/refund`: full refund, then reject.

Notes:
- UltraCart will not re-send a Rejected order to the fulfillment center.  An order is only retransmitted if someone moves
  it back into the Shipping Department with retransmit checked, or clicks Retransmit.
- `POST /order/orders/{order_id}/cancel` is not used here.  It fails once an order is queued for or transmitted to a
  fulfillment center, which is the case for an order waiting in the Shipping Department.
- `auto_order_cancel=false` leaves the auto order (if the order came from one) alone.  Cancel it separately if needed.

**Step 1. Retrieve the order \[[Create API Key](https://ultracart.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ucdoc/pages/38688545/API+Simple+Key)\]**
```bash
curl -X GET "https://secure.ultracart.com/rest/v2/order/orders/DEMO-0009104436?_expand=item,shipping,summary,auto_order" \
  -H "Accept: application/json" \
  -H "X-UltraCart-Api-Version: 2017-03-01" \
  -H "x-ultracart-simple-key: 55f7c4940f843d01a10c5d77f17001009dcc02345e79bd01a10c5d77f1700100"
```

**Response Body** (abbreviated: check these fields)
```json
{
    "order": {
        "order_id": "DEMO-0009104436",
        "current_stage": "Shipping Department",
        "items": [ ... ],
        "shipping": {
            "tracking_numbers": [],
            ...
        },
        "summary": { ... },
        ...
    },
    "success": true
}
```

**Step 2. Make sure the order is refundable**
```bash
curl -X GET "https://secure.ultracart.com/rest/v2/order/orders/DEMO-0009104436/refundable" \
  -H "Accept: application/json" \
  -H "X-UltraCart-Api-Version: 2017-03-01" \
  -H "x-ultracart-simple-key: 55f7c4940f843d01a10c5d77f17001009dcc02345e79bd01a10c5d77f1700100"
```

**Response Body** (abbreviated)
```json
{
    "refundable": true,
    "order_level_refund_reasons": [ ... ],
    "success": true
}
```

**Step 3. Unless ShipStation cancels the order for you (see above), cancel it at your fulfillment provider.  Stop here if it refuses.**

**Step 4. Refund in full and reject**

Send back the whole order from step 1 with the refunded fields set.  These are TOTAL amounts (positive numbers), not
deltas.  For a full refund:
- each item: `quantity_refunded` = `quantity`, `total_refunded` = `total_cost_with_discount`
- `summary.tax_refunded` = `summary.tax`
- `summary.shipping_handling_refunded` = `summary.shipping_handling_total`

A refund reason may be required by your account (Home -> Configuration -> Order Management -> Refund/Reject Reasons).
If so, also set `refund_reason` on the order.

```bash
curl -X PUT "https://secure.ultracart.com/rest/v2/order/orders/DEMO-0009104436/refund\
?reject_after_refund=true&skip_customer_notification=false&auto_order_cancel=false&manual_refund=false&reverse_affiliate_transactions=true&issue_store_credit=false&_expand=item,summary" \
  -H "Accept: application/json" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8" \
  -H "X-UltraCart-Api-Version: 2017-03-01" \
  -H "x-ultracart-simple-key: 55f7c4940f843d01a10c5d77f17001009dcc02345e79bd01a10c5d77f1700100" \
  -d $'{
    "order_id": "DEMO-0009104436",
    "current_stage": "Shipping Department",
    "items": [
        {
            "item_reference_oid": 127545010,
            "merchant_item_id": "BONE",
            "quantity": 1.0,
            "quantity_refunded": 1.0,
            "total_cost_with_discount": { "value": 17.95, "currency_code": "USD" },
            "total_refunded": { "value": 17.95, "currency_code": "USD" },
            ...
        }
    ],
    "summary": {
        "tax": { "value": 0.0, "currency_code": "USD" },
        "tax_refunded": { "value": 0.0, "currency_code": "USD" },
        "shipping_handling_total": { "value": 5.00, "currency_code": "USD" },
        "shipping_handling_refunded": { "value": 5.00, "currency_code": "USD" },
        ...
    },
    ...
}'
```

| Query parameter | Value | Why |
|---|---|---|
| `reject_after_refund` | `true` | Moves the order out of the Shipping Department into Rejected |
| `skip_customer_notification` | `false` | Let the customer know their refund is on the way |
| `auto_order_cancel` | `false` | Leave the auto order (if any) alone |
| `manual_refund` | `false` | Refund through the payment gateway, to the original payment method |
| `reverse_affiliate_transactions` | `true` | No affiliate commission on a cancelled order |
| `issue_store_credit` | `false` | Money back, not store credit |

**Response Body** (abbreviated)
```json
{
    "order": {
        "order_id": "DEMO-0009104436",
        "current_stage": "Rejected",
        "summary": {
            "total_refunded": { "value": 22.95, ... },
            ...
        },
        ...
    },
    "success": true
}
```

**Error Response Body**

`Request to refund an invalid amount.` means the refund total came out as zero or less.
```json
{
    "error": {
        "developer_message": "Request to refund an invalid amount.",
        "user_message": "Request to refund an invalid amount."
    },
    "success": false
}
```
